OL,2,Wj5{5jj5s1FPAISLEY HAS 'FRANK'
OL,3,W/*%/,$/..%,.%FMEETING WITH TRIMBLE
OL,4,G`````````````
OL,5,FThe new Ulster Unionist Party leader,
OL,6,FDavid Trimble, had his first meeting
OL,7,Ftoday with DUP leader Ian Paisley.
OL,8,F
OL,9,GAfterwards both men agreed that their
OL,10, talks - at Dr Paisley's home - had been
OL,11, frank but friendly, although the Ulster
OL,12, Unionist leader would not commit
OL,13, himself to a voting pact at Westminster
OL,15, Mr Trimble is to see John Major
OL,16, tomorrow and said he would soon be
OL,17, arranging meetings with John Bruton and
OL,18, party leaders in the Republic.
OL,20, Earlier, the DUP leader dismissed the
OL,21, establishment of a single Unionist
OL,22, party as proposed by David Trimble.
OL,23,V]DFrom 18-09-95   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
